### What Is a Super Flag Bet?
A Super Flag consists of five selections that generate 46 individual bets through multiple combinations. The structure builds from paired selections upward: 10 doubles combine any two selections, 10 trebles use any three, 5 fourfolds take any four selections, and 1 fivefold combines all five. The additional 10 Single Stakes About bets distinguish the Flag bet from standard accumulators, pairing selections with protective conditional stakes.
Horse racing represents the most common application for Super Flag bets, where punters select five horses across different races. Football markets also support this bet type when players identify five matches for accumulator coverage. The 46-bet total means a £1 stake per bet requires £46 total stake, making stake calculation essential before placement.
