## Each Way Super Flag Betting
Each Way betting transforms a Super Flag from 46 bets into 92 individual wagers by adding place components to every selection. This doubles the total stake but provides significant insurance, particularly in horse racing where place terms apply. The Super Flag Calculator handles the complexity of combined win and place returns, calculating how different finishing positions affect overall profit across all 46 bet combinations within the Flag bet structure.
### Each Way Terms and Place Payouts
Place terms determine how much bettors receive when selections finish in placed positions rather than winning outright. Standard terms typically offer 1/5 of the win odds for races with eight or more runners, paying the top three places. Races with five to seven runners usually pay 1/4 odds for the top two places. These terms vary between bookmakers and race types, with some offering enhanced place terms as promotions. The Super Flag Calculator applies these place fractions to each of the 5 selections, then calculates returns across all doubles, trebles, fourfolds and the Accumulator, generating a complete picture of potential place payouts alongside win returns.
### Calculating Each Way Returns
When selections place but don't win, Each Way bets generate returns that offset losses from unsuccessful combinations. For example, if three of five selections place at 1/5 odds, the 10 doubles involving those three still produce returns, though at reduced fractions. Super Flag Calculator processes both the win side and place side simultaneously, showing how even partial success delivers profit. The system accounts for scenarios where some selections win while others only place, calculating the exact return for each of the 46 win bets and 46 place bets. This complexity makes manual calculation impractical, but the calculator delivers instant accuracy across all 92 wagers.
